In the JSON-LD structured data implementation for product reviews, the `author.name` property generates an empty string (`"name": ""`) when a review is submitted by a guest user or a customer without a stored name.

Google's Structured Data guidelines require the `name `property within the `Person `schema to contain a non-empty string. When this value is empty, Google Search Console flags it as a critical error: `Missing field "name" (in "review.author")`, which prevents the product from properly validating for Rich Snippets.

```
"review": [
  {
    "@type": "Review",
    "author": {
      "@type": "Person",
      "name": ""
    }
  }
]
```

It should be "Guest"

nopSolutions/nopCommerce:7705.body:
If you review SearchProductsAsync in ProductService:
 https://github.com/nopSolutions/nopCommerce/blob/402ed11ee4dea8d9d2904ddb7a0463f24d06f216/src/Libraries/Nop.Services/Catalog/ProductService.cs#L1167-L1180
You can see that the Pagination is applied _before_ the providers ordering/sorting is applied. If you apply a large page size (such that all items are on one page) you will see that sorting is applied correctly, but on smaller page sizes, where results are truncated prior to ordering, the sort order is incorrect.

Something like the following would fix it and maintains ToPageListAsync optimization and function surface.
```csharp

var products = productsQuery.OrderBy(_localizedPropertyRepository, await _workContext.GetWorkingLanguageAsync(), orderBy);

if (providerResults.Any() && orderBy == ProductSortingEnum.Position && !showHidden)
{
    var orderDict = providerResults.Select((value, index) => new { value, index }).ToDictionary(x => x.value, x => x.index);
    products = from item in products               
               join sortOrder in orderDict on item.Id equals sortOrder.Key
               orderby sortOrder.Value
               select item;
}

return await products.ToPagedListAsync(pageIndex, pageSize);
```
The only issue with this implementation is that items that are in the products query but not in the provider results will be ignored/lost.
